title A guard is the wrong unit for a skip -- %446 closed at the four legs rather than at the roster row
prompt the baton, unattended -- bakery lap 3998, rota row 3
rota lap 3998, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes. Care and flow, and taste only works up close: read the actual file, run the actual witness. The row's own discipline decided this lap. The card and the ledger both said the launch was the guard's LAST leg, and one run of the scan showed it is the fourth of seven -- a fact no amount of reading the row would have produced.
think Opened with fleet_round_open.sh, already on the anointed order at 59e7179176. Read the card whole, the rota row, and the previous lap's recommend line. That log named the mktemp probe as its next door; I took %446 instead, because it is this pier's only red and a red books the allocation before new work.
think Lindy-first and crux-first both point at %446 rather than at mktemp. It is the sole red on this roster, so it alone withholds roster_receipt_write, which is what --scoped needs; every ship on this pier therefore pays a full ~814s cold pass every lap for a reading that is not about the tree. Fixing the seam under the witness harness is my lane, and it is the hardest still-solvable item in it.
think Measured before designing. bwrap resolves to bubblewrap-0.11.2, bwrap --ro-bind / / true exits 1 with Failed to make / slave: Operation not permitted, unshare --mount true exits 1 the same way, and /proc/self/status reads NoNewPrivs 1 / Seccomp 2 -- the peer's diagnosis reproduces exactly.
think Then ran the scan itself rather than trusting the row's account of it, and that one run changed the whole repair. The row says the LAST leg launches the jail. It is the FOURTH of seven, and three legs pass green before it -- including the claude.json leg that REDS %408 exists for, which is the only reading this guard has ever caught a real fault with here.
think So the roster capability field, which the row calls the mechanism and already built, is the wrong instrument. It can only answer whole guards, and skipping this guard would have silently dropped three legs that work in order to excuse four that cannot -- the roster's own quietly-thinning hazard, one level down, arriving through the very field written to prevent it.
think Put the refusal at the legs instead. tools/fixtures/m/mount_namespace_probe.sh holds one sourceable function, mount_namespace_state, returning present, absent, or unknown; agent_jail_witness.sh sources it after leg three and, on absent alone, prints four named SKIP lines and closes green. Three legs still assert on every jailed lap.
think Carried the nuance the row named rather than rediscovering it: command -v bwrap is asked FIRST, so a pier without bubblewrap reads unknown and reds honestly, since agent-jail.sh cannot run there either. Only bwrap's own Operation not permitted reads absent. The exit code alone can never decide this, which is why the refusal text is read.
obs A GUARD IS THE WRONG UNIT FOR A SKIP WHEN ITS LEGS NEED DIFFERENT INSTRUMENTS. That is the transferable half. The capability tier is honest for a guard whose legs all ask one question -- comlink_r1_dual_stack needs IPv6 for the whole of itself -- and dishonest for one whose legs ask several, because the roster's vocabulary has no word smaller than a guard.
obs THE ROW'S OWN DIAGNOSIS WAS ONE WORD OFF AND THE WORD MATTERED. last leg versus fourth of seven is the difference between a capability row and a leg-level refusal, and between keeping the %408 reading and losing it. The peer wrote a careful, measured row from inside a jail; what it could not do from there was watch the scan reach leg four and stop.
obs MY FIRST CONTROL LEG MEASURED PROSE INSTEAD OF BEHAVIOR. witness_spells_no_second_probe grepped the whole witness for bwrap and refused it for explaining itself in a comment. The reading I wanted is command position, so it strips comment and echo lines now -- and I proved the fixed leg still bites by appending a real bwrap call to a copy.
obs EVERY ANSWER PLANTED WITH A REAL FAKE bwrap ON PATH, NOT A FLAG. An override env var would have been a bypass door standing beside the skip forever; a pen directory first on PATH proves the same three answers through the function that actually ships, command -v included. Two of the three answers must NOT skip, and both are shown reaching the launch legs.
obs THE THREE ANSWERS ARE PROVEN DISTINCT. Two of them are unknown by design, so a probe that returned one word for everything would have satisfied each individual leg that wanted that word. The distinctness leg is what makes the other four mean anything.
obs THE ROSTER SCAN STILL READS RED FROM THE RECORDED RUN. standing_equipment_scan reports runs_red=1 agent_jail from the 20260906.003354 pass, which ran before this repair. The record moves when a pass re-runs the guard, which is what the hot close is for -- a reading about the last pass rather than about the tree as it now stands.
obs I DECLINED THE MECHANISM THE CARD OFFERED AND SAID SO IN THREE PLACES. The roster row now carries a NO capability FIELD, DELIBERATELY paragraph, because the next hand to read that row will reach for the field the ledger recommended, and the reason it is wrong here is a measurement rather than a taste.
loom witness=agent_jail_witness legs_proven=3 legs_skipped=4 control_checks=17 control_failures=0 wall_s=1.9
loom hot_pass=standing_equipment guards=124 green=120 red=0 gated=4 wall_s=800 receipt=written
loom hot_pass_first=standing_equipment guards=124 green=119 red=1 gated=4 wall_s=906 red_guard=log_has_a_row
loom probe=mount_namespace_state refusing_wall_ms=3 answers=3
file tools/fixtures/m/mount_namespace_probe.sh one sourceable function, three answers, and the bwrap-missing nuance read before the exit code
file tools/ag/agent_jail_witness.sh sources the probe after leg three; on a positively read absence names four skipped legs and closes green
file tools/ag/agent_jail_witness.rish runs the control beside the scan and asserts the five readings that keep the skip a skip
file tools/fixtures/a/agent_jail_control.sh 17 legs -- three probe answers planted with a fake bwrap on PATH, both non-skipping answers shown reaching the launch legs
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the agent_jail row says why it carries no capability field, so the next hand does not add one
file construction/REDS.md %446 closed, the capability field declined on a measurement, the last-leg claim corrected
file construction/ITINERARY.md the live front reads CLOSED and this pier's red count reaches zero
obs THE FIRST HOT PASS READ agent_jail GREEN IN 2s AND STILL WITHHELD THE RECEIPT, because a SECOND guard had gone red in the window: log_has_a_row, on a pin count rather than on my work. The living pin said the 20260905 shelf held 56 logs and the shelf and its index both held 58, two peer laps having landed after the pin's row was written. One number, measured off disk both ways before it moved.
obs NO REDS ROW FOR THAT ONE. The guard existed, ran on schedule, and named the drift the lap it appeared -- which is the designed behavior rather than a defect nothing was reading. A ratchet turns on touch and books nothing; booking it would spend a ledger number on an instrument working.
obs THE RECEIPT WRITES. Second hot pass, 124 guards, 120 green, ZERO red, 4 gated at their custody doors, 800s -- and construction/standing-equipment-receipt.kyri now carries scope full at head 59e7179176. That file is the whole point of the lap: --scoped refuses without a full green receipt, so until this pass every ship on this pier paid ~800s of full roster every lap. The fusion opens here.
obs THE ORDERING DEFECT DID NOT FIRE ON MY OWN SEND, AND I ALMOST WROTE THAT IT DID. I staged first, regenerated, and expected the witness count to move; both pages came back byte-identical, because readme_metrics counts *_witness paths and my two new files are fixtures under tools/fixtures/. The recommend line had already claimed this send as evidence before I checked the diff. A claim about my own round is exactly as checkable as any other, and this one was wrong.
recommend kg -- the baton's SEND clause is the next door, and this send is NOT its evidence: I regenerated after staging expecting a moved count and both pages were already current, since readme_metrics counts *_witness paths and my two new files are fixtures. The card's own 1806/1807 measurement stands; mine adds nothing to it. Two words, eight ships.
